This setter isn't on the decode hot path, so a speedup is unlikely. The rewrite is behavior-identical: the only change is that the literal arguments are written as explicitly typed constants, which avoids implicit integer conversions at the call site.

```cpp
    void SetAwakeningsCount(FIT_UINT8 awakeningsCount)
    {
        SetFieldUINT8Value(static_cast<FIT_UINT8>(11), awakeningsCount, static_cast<FIT_UINT8>(0), static_cast<FIT_UINT16>(FIT_SUBFIELD_INDEX_MAIN_FIELD));
    }
```